title: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened › Where the denial is weak
route: /denials?id=D-3318
intro: The findings card: each finding has a severity, a source chip that opens the chart excerpt, and a suggested fix that can be added to the evidence for the brief and the appeal.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Scroll to 'Where the denial is weak'"
process p0 "Words of the card follow the denial type\nPartial approval, Level-of-care downgrade, Units cut, Late notice, Retro-authorization denied, Full denial\nD-3318 is written out in full"
screen sc1 "'Where the denial is weak'\n'Each finding links to the chart, with a suggested fix'"
screen f1 "One row per finding\nSeverity pill 'Critical' or 'Strong', title, detail"
screen f2 "Under it: source chip (for example 'Progress note 10/14'), 'Suggested fix: Add the progress note from 10/14', button 'Add to the evidence'"

click c1 "Click the source chip"
overlay o1 "Drawer titled with the source name\n'From the chart. Reader found this and removed identifiers.'"
doc dc1 "Paper sheet\n'Clinical record excerpt', 'Identifiers removed', title, Member and Program\nThe excerpt is highlighted"
click c2 "Close: click X, press Esc, or click the dimmed area"
end e1 "Back on the page, nothing changed"

click c3 "Click 'Add to the evidence'"
store st1 "Fix saved on this denial"
process p1 "Button turns to a tick and reads 'Added to the evidence'"
click c4 "Click 'Added to the evidence' again"
store st2 "Fix removed from this denial"
process p2 "Button reads 'Add to the evidence' again"

process p3 "Brief page: the fix is listed under 'Have these open'\nunless it only repeats a source already listed"
process p4 "Appeal letter drawer: the fix is listed under 'Evidence to attach' and ticked"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › The brief"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Written appeal › Confirm and draft"
process p5 "Added fixes stay for the session\nThey do not change the win chance"

s1 --> sc1
p0 --> sc1
sc1 --> f1 --> f2
f2 --> c1 --> o1 --> dc1 --> c2 --> e1
f2 --> c3 --> st1 --> p1 --> c4 --> st2 --> p2
p1 --> p3 --> g1
p1 --> p4 --> g2
st1 -.-> p5
